id: pm-jira-h5wu
title: "Decision: hook policy (best-effort, opt-in, no auto-push)"
description: ""
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-06-03T05:18:55.681Z"
updated_at: "2026-06-03T05:18:55.681Z"
author: codex
body: "onWrite is registered always (so 'hooks' capability is genuinely used) but is a strict no-op unless PM_JIRA_PUSH_ON_WRITE is truthy AND creds present. Even when enabled it does NOT auto-POST to Jira: the onWrite ctx only yields {path,scope,op} (no item body), and auto-pushing every write risks spamming/duplicating upstream issues. Real upstream sync stays the explicit, reviewable 'pm jira export --push'. Hook is the opt-in, testable surface; logic isolated in pure decidePushOnWrite."
